{
  "kind": "hurt8",
  "comment": "Pose guides for the 8-direction, 4-frame hurt sheet; conventions as walk8.json. Four frames of recoil and settle, struck from the front: impact drives the chest back while the hips lag forward, frame 1 is the deepest point of the arch with the rear foot staggered back and the head thrown behind the shoulder line, frame 2 comes back up still crouched, and frame 3 settles a hair below the idle stance. The arms fly out sideways as much as backwards, which is what makes the recoil legible in the rows that face the camera, where a backwards lean projects to almost nothing.",
